  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tPayroll\n\t\tPayroll FAQs\n\n### The PDF is asking me for a password to open the payslips. How do we set the password?\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Tue, 26 Mar, 2019 at  1:24 PM\n\n\t\tUnder the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) requirements, Capium is protecting payslip with password protection. \n\nYou may find the payslip password under the employee details action drop-down edit personal details and it is the default, System Generated.\n\nPlease refer below screenshot for more help.\n\nClick here to watch how to change your payslip template\n\nClick here to watch how to setup a payslip password\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
  "bodyHtml": "\n\t<div class=\"breadcrumb\">\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions\"> Solution home </a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/9000115223\">Payroll</a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/folders/9000188558\">Payroll FAQs</a>\n\t</div>\n\t<b class=\"page-stamp page-stamp-article\">\n\t\t<b class=\"icon-page-article\"></b>\n\t</b>\n\n\t<h2 class=\"heading\">The PDF is asking me for a password to open the payslips. How do we set the password?\n\t \t<a href=\"#\"\n            class=\"solution-print--icon print--remove\"\n \t\t\ttitle=\"Print this Article\"\n \t\t\tarial-role=\"link\"\n \t\t\tarial-label=\"Print this Article\"\n\t\t\tid=\"print-article\"\n \t\t>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"icon-print\"></span>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"text-print\">Print</span>\n \t\t</a>\n\t</h2>\n\t\n\t<p>Modified on: Tue, 26 Mar, 2019 at  1:24 PM</p>\n\t<hr />\n\t\n\n\t<article class=\"article-body\" id=\"article-body\" rel=\"image-enlarge\">\n\t\t<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) requirements, Capium is protecting payslip with password protection. </span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">You may find the payslip password under the employee details action drop-down edit personal details and it is the default, System Generated.<br><br>Please refer below screenshot for more help.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9074214688/original/R2DF6s6ciXZa-sZStFKZylGGMbkdTVgl3w.png?1553596932\" class=\"fr-fic fr-dii\" data-filelink=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9074214688/original/R2DF6s6ciXZa-sZStFKZylGGMbkdTVgl3w.png?1553596932\" data-fileid=\"9074214688\" data-uniquekey=\"1553596922028\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9074214689/original/bCJxMTZylPiFICnR5UBEFe71GtcgNYyfWw.png?1553596932\" class=\"fr-fic fr-dii\" data-filelink=\"https://s3.